import json
from pathlib import Path
p=json.loads(Path('documentation_revision/current-paragraphs.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
ed=[]
def change(old,new,count=1):ed.append({'find':old,'replacement':new,'expected':count})
def para(i,t):change(p[i],t)
para(261,'This chapter presents the routing model, rainfall advisory, supporting concepts, related studies, and system architecture. The equations define how recorded road conditions affect route cost, while the advisory communicates model-estimated rainfall separately.')
para(263,'BARANGAYAN combines Dijkstra evacuation routing with an Open-Meteo rainfall advisory for Barangay Ampid I. Routing selects the available center with the lowest flood-weighted path cost for the chosen transport mode. Published closures, recorded depths, blocked-road marks, and center availability determine the route. Rainfall estimates are displayed separately and do not predict street flooding. The Historical Weather API supports test preparation only. Related routing and warning studies inform this design; the study does not claim worldwide priority or independently established forecast accuracy (Piamonte et al., 2026; Ogawa et al., 2023; Young et al., 2021; Zippenfenig, 2023).')
para(280,'D(e) = the recorded historical depth of segment e, in metres. A measured zero and an unknown value must remain distinct. The current zero fallback for missing records does not establish that a street is dry; routes using it require a visible data limitation.')
para(665,'D(e) / Dmax,m for a recorded depth. The current zero fallback for missing data is labelled unknown and is not evidence of a dry road.')
para(809,'The reviewed studies support combining resident services with flood-weighted routing and a separate rainfall advisory. BARANGAYAN applies this design to Ampid I through Android and resident websites, a staff website, and a shared Supabase backend. Its contribution is local integration. Usability, route correctness, geographic accuracy, and service reliability require separate evaluation; findings from other places do not establish performance in Ampid I.')
para(997,'Presentation tier. The resident Android application and website provide personal accounts, service requests, reports, maps, payments, health registration, and emergency information. The staff website provides assigned processing, content management, and administrative summaries. Server and database checks enforce the permission matrix in Table 13.')
change('RESIDENTS (MOBILE MODULE)','RESIDENT ANDROID APPLICATION')
change('PAGASA warning colour','Application display colour')
change('the advisory limits follow the PAGASA warning bands and are set by the barangay.','the application thresholds are informed by rainfall-intensity classes and require barangay DRRM review.')
change('Open-Meteo, n.d.','Open-Meteo, n.d.-a',3)
change('not an accuracy ranking (Open-Meteo, n.d.-a; OpenWeather, n.d.; WeatherAPI.com, n.d.).','not an accuracy ranking (Open-Meteo, n.d.-b; OpenWeather, n.d.; WeatherAPI.com, n.d.).')
change('Assigned staff and administrator','Administrator',2)
change('Staff web permission matrix: Clerk/secretary—residency review, requests and print preview; health worker—drives and registrations; tanod/incident staff—incident review; treasurer—payment records; content staff—announcements and archives; administrator—accounts and configuration. Each assignment requires server and database enforcement; unassigned actions are denied.','Staff web: manage accounts, role assignments, and system configuration. Operational actions require the appropriate permission; unassigned actions are denied by the server and database.')
change('The QR check-in, Family, and Alerts screens allow residents to access check-in codes, manage household members, and view barangay emergency announcements.','These prototype screens show QR check-in codes, household records, and emergency announcements. Scan validity, relationship rules, and alert sound require the acceptance tests in Table 15a.')
change('The Staff and Admin Accounts screen allows administrators to manage staff accounts, assigned roles, and account status.','The Staff and Admin Accounts screen shows account roles and status. Server and database permissions must match Table 13 and pass unauthorized-access tests.')
change('The Requirements and Guidelines panel displays the requirements, fee, and processing information for the selected document.','The Requirements and Guidelines panel shows the selected document’s requirements, fee, and processing information. Residency-proof review and print preview require separate interface and test evidence.')
Path('documentation_revision/followups.json').write_text(json.dumps(ed,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
print(len(ed))
